  "body": "Found while fixing the review of PR #1522 (#1504).\n\nWhat happens: a plain Slot whose source is a whole model (`SrcRef::Entity(\"part\")`) or the stock takes no part law: `depth_law_of` (`crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs`, the `_ => DepthLaw::None` arm) gives a Slot `DepthLaw::Section` only when its source is a Selection. So a typed slot through the part's pocket wall generates and posts with no gouge warning, even when the job knows the source model is the finished part (`part_solid` is true). It is pinned as today's behaviour by `with_nothing_picked_the_typed_endpoints_rule_as_before` in `crates/app/tests/slot_picks.rs`: Entity(\"part\") source, slot (-20,0)-(20,0) width 12 cut through the 30 x 16 pocket's walls at x 15, no `Warning::Gouge`.\n\nWhy P1: #1504's own third bullet (the maintainer's report) expects \"With nothing selected, the typed endpoints still work, and the model gouge check still decides.\" Today nothing decides, so a gouge into the finished part passes to the post. The code comment's contract (\"the source is the material to remove, not a part to keep\") holds for a Stock source, but not when the named model is the finished part.\n\nExpected: with an entity source that is the finished part, the Slot is judged against it (`DepthLaw::Section`, as for a picked Slot) and a slot through a wall is convicted as a blocking Gouge. A Stock source keeps today's behaviour. The same question applies to Circular (same arm); decide it with this issue or file it separately.\n\nDone means: a test with an Entity(\"part\") Slot cut through the pocket wall gets a blocking `Warning::Gouge` and the post is held; a Stock source still cuts the typed slot unjudged; `with_nothing_picked_the_typed_endpoints_rule_as_before` is updated to the new law.\n\nRefs #1504\n",
